details.image_prompt:
{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition is centered with generous negative space, framed at a 3/4 overhead angle to clearly display the entirety of the ingredients. The depth of field is shallow, keeping the foreground serving sharp while the second plate behind it is softly blurred. Soft natural side light from a window to the left creates subtle, gentle shadows and a slight sheen on the light soy-based glaze. The scene is set on an aged, dark oak tabletop with visible wood grain. Placed naturally on the table are a wooden spatula and a few loose toasted sesame seeds and a fragment of a bok choy leaf. The dish consists of two simple, matte ceramic plates. Each plate features a base of steaming brown rice, topped with tender, five-spice coated turkey strips and a vibrant mix of bright green snap peas and softened baby bok choy. The turkey is browned and aromatic, positioned next to the glistening vegetables rather than buried. A light, savory glaze coats the ingredients. A scattering of toasted sesame seeds is unevenly sprinkled over the top. The overall color palette is warm and inviting, showing natural, cooked textures like the caramelization on the turkey and the vivid, tender greens of the bok choy. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Include slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish, a small, accidental sauce drip on the plate rim, and a few stray sesame seeds on the wood surface. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography."
}
